**Read:** [Water stewardship — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Mine-Water-Stewardship-Handbook.lingua#r_4Y8Q03RFJBVBN6WVVY3EN6Q5DM), the entire handbook; [Usinas de Beneficiamento de Minérios do Brasil — CETEM](../sources/CETEM-Usinas-de-Beneficiamento.lingua#r_62ZD994C9YYXB1YDVFQST5B27J), a complete selected plant/water case; [Tratamento de Minérios — CETEM, sixth edition](../sources/Tratamento-de-Minerios-CETEM.lingua#r_04ZQFADZ3NC3T6QDPQ565W1ERA), the full slurry, dewatering, and stream-basis treatments; [Engineering Geology Field Manual — U.S. Bureau of Reclamation](../sources/USBR-Engineering-Geology-Field-Manual.lingua#r_5WS5PNK19008B3SV6D1WWNVTRE), the full relevant water measurement methods.

A mine/process water balance includes inflows, outflows, transfers, storage, rainfall/runoff, infiltration, evaporation, process moisture, reuse, seepage, and other identified terms over a specified period and boundary. Internal recycle changes equipment flows without becoming new external water supply.

Wet and dry material quantities, water density, moisture basis, and inventory changes must be consistent. Tailings, concentrate, backfill, dust control, cooling, and drainage can carry water across boundaries. A steady-state assumption should be tested against storage and seasonal/operating variation.

Measurement and model uncertainties can be correlated. Forcing closure by one balancing term can conceal meter bias, unobserved seepage, timing mismatch, or storage error. Preserve raw observations and distinguish a reconciled estimate from a direct measurement.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete water-account case from the handbook and plant study. Independently close quantities with explicit stocks/flows and support periods, then test a storage, weather, or production-change scenario. Compare two explanations for a consequential mismatch and identify the observation needed to discriminate them.

Read the entire water-stewardship handbook and full relevant processing/field methods. The next quality step adds constituents and reactions; volume closure alone cannot establish a suitable reuse or discharge stream.

**Continue:** [Join water quantities with constituents, reactions, and intended use](Water-quality-reuse-reactions-and-discharge-evidence.lingua#r_0EW72C79PC40WD3VNQKSYM5PSN).

